  <section id="wissenai-preprocess-package">
<h1>wissenai.preprocess package<a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai-preprocess-package" title="Link to this heading"></a></h1>

<section id="module-wissenai.preprocess.pdf_miner_process">
<span id="wissenai-preprocess-pdf-miner-process-module"></span><h2>wissenai.preprocess.pdf_miner_process module<a class="headerlink" href="#module-wissenai.preprocess.pdf_miner_process" title="Link to this heading"></a></h2>
<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.pdf_miner_process.extract_text_with_bbox">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.pdf_miner_process.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">extract_text_with_bbox</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">file_path</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">pdf_name</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/pdf_miner_process.html#extract_text_with_bbox"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.pdf_miner_process.extract_text_with_bbox" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>file_path (str): Path to the input PDF file.
pdf_name (str): Name or identifier of the PDF file, stored for reference in each text block.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><dl class="simple">
<dt>dict: A dictionary mapping page numbers (int) to a list of dictionaries,</dt><dd><dl class="simple">
<dt>each containing:</dt><dd><ul class="simple">
<li><p>“text_block_id” (int): ID of the text line within the element.</p></li>
<li><p>“element_id” (int): ID of the text element (LTTextBoxHorizontal).</p></li>
<li><p>“text” (str): The extracted text string.</p></li>
<li><p>“pdf_name” (str): The provided PDF name/identifier.</p></li>
<li><p>“bbox” (dict): Bounding box with keys “x0”, “y0”, “x1”, “y1” transformed to top-left origin.</p></li>
<li><p>“page_number” (int): Page number (1-indexed).</p></li>
<li><p>“page_width” (float): Width of the page in points.</p></li>
<li><p>“page_height” (float): Height of the page in points.</p></li>
</ul>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>


</section>
<section id="module-wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf">
<span id="wissenai-preprocess-searchable-pdf-module"></span><h2>wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf module<a class="headerlink" href="#module-wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf" title="Link to this heading"></a></h2>
<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.convert_pdf_to_images">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">convert_pdf_to_images</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">file_path</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">batch_size</span></span><span class="o"><span class="pre">=</span></span><span class="default_value"><span class="pre">20</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">dpi</span></span><span class="o"><span class="pre">=</span></span><span class="default_value"><span class="pre">300</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/searchable_pdf.html#convert_pdf_to_images"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.convert_pdf_to_images" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Converts a PDF file into a generator that yields batches of page images.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>file_path (str): Path to the input PDF file.
batch_size (int, optional): Number of pages per batch. Defaults to 20.
dpi (int, optional): Resolution in DPI for image rendering. Defaults to 300.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>generator: Generator yielding lists of PIL Images per batch.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.create_searchable_pdf_pipeline">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">create_searchable_pdf_pipeline</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">file_name</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">file_path</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">output_directory_path</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/searchable_pdf.html#create_searchable_pdf_pipeline"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.create_searchable_pdf_pipeline" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Full pipeline to check if a PDF is searchable, convert non-searchable PDFs 
to searchable using OCR, and save the result.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>file_name (str): Name of the PDF file (without path).
file_path (str): Full path to the PDF file.
output_directory_path (str): Directory to store processed outputs.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><dl class="simple">
<dt>str: Path to the final searchable PDF (original if already searchable, </dt><dd><p>or newly created if not).</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.enhance_dpi">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">enhance_dpi</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">pil_image</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">new_dpi</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">old_dpi</span></span><span class="o"><span class="pre">=</span></span><span class="default_value"><span class="pre">150</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/searchable_pdf.html#enhance_dpi"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.enhance_dpi" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Enhances the resolution (DPI) of a PIL image.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>pil_image (PIL.Image): Image to be resized.
new_dpi (int): Desired DPI.
old_dpi (int, optional): Original DPI. Defaults to 150.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>PIL.Image: Resized image with enhanced DPI.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.enhance_image_for_ocr">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">enhance_image_for_ocr</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">image</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/searchable_pdf.html#enhance_image_for_ocr"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.enhance_image_for_ocr" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Enhances an image for better OCR performance using grayscale and thresholding.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>image (np.ndarray): OpenCV image (NumPy array) in BGR format.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>np.ndarray: Enhanced binary image.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.extract_images_from_pdf">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">extract_images_from_pdf</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">pdf_path</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/searchable_pdf.html#extract_images_from_pdf"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.extract_images_from_pdf" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Extracts images from each page of a PDF, applies denoising and DPI enhancement.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>pdf_path (str): Path to the input PDF file.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>list: List of tuples (PIL.Image, page_number) for each page.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.get_file_name_without_extension">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">get_file_name_without_extension</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">file_path</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/searchable_pdf.html#get_file_name_without_extension"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.get_file_name_without_extension" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd></dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.is_searchable_pdf">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">is_searchable_pdf</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">file_path</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/searchable_pdf.html#is_searchable_pdf"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.is_searchable_pdf" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Checks if a PDF file is searchable by attempting to extract text.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>file_path (str): Path to the PDF file.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>bool: True if the PDF contains searchable text, False otherwise.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.make_searchable_pdf">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">make_searchable_pdf</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">images</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">file_name</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">output_directory</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/searchable_pdf.html#make_searchable_pdf"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.make_searchable_pdf" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Creates a searchable PDF by performing OCR on images and combining them.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>images (list): List of tuples (PIL.Image, page_number) representing each page.
file_name (str): Base name for the output PDF.
output_directory (str): Directory to save the output searchable PDF.</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>str: Path to the final searchable PDF file.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.pdf_to_html">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">pdf_to_html</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">pdf_path</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">html_path</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/searchable_pdf.html#pdf_to_html"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.pdf_to_html" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Converts the text content of a searchable PDF into an HTML file.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>pdf_path (str): Path to the input PDF file.
html_path (str): Output path for the HTML file.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.pdf_to_markdown">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">pdf_to_markdown</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">pdf_path</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">markdown_path</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/searchable_pdf.html#pdf_to_markdown"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.pdf_to_markdown" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Converts the text content of a searchable PDF into a Markdown file.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>pdf_path (str): Path to the input PDF file.
markdown_path (str): Output path for the Markdown file.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.perform_ocr">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">perform_ocr</span></span><span class="sig-paren">(</span><em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">image</span></span></em>, <em class="sig-param"><span class="n"><span class="pre">dpi</span></span><span class="o"><span class="pre">=</span></span><span class="default_value"><span class="pre">300</span></span></em><span class="sig-paren">)</span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/searchable_pdf.html#perform_ocr"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.searchable_pdf.perform_ocr" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Performs OCR on an image with optional preprocessing using OpenCV.</p>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Args:</dt><dd><p>image: The OpenCV image object (numpy array).
dpi: Desired dots-per-inch for the final PIL image (default 300).</p>
</dd>
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>The OCR result as HOCR (HTML).</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

</section>
<section id="module-wissenai.preprocess.utils">
<span id="wissenai-preprocess-utils-module"></span><h2>wissenai.preprocess.utils module<a class="headerlink" href="#module-wissenai.preprocess.utils" title="Link to this heading"></a></h2>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.utils.get_file_type">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.utils.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">get_file_type</span></span></span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/utils.html#adaptive_threshold"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.utils.adaptive_threshold" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Detects the file type based on its extension or MIME type.
Args:</p>
<blockquote>
<div><p>file_path (str): Path of the input file.</p>
</div></blockquote>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>str:'PDF', 'Image', 'Text', etc..</p>

</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.utils.detect_languages">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.utils.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">detect_languages</span></span></span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/utils.html#adaptive_threshold"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.utils.adaptive_threshold" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Detects languages from a list of text strings (one per page).
Args:</p>
<blockquote>
<div><p>texts (list): List of input texts.
        min_chars (int): Minimum number of characters for language to be detected</p>
</div></blockquote>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>set: Set of full names of detected languages.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.utils.derasterize">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.utils.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">derasterize</span></span></span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/utils.html#adaptive_threshold"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.utils.adaptive_threshold" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Derasterize scanned image by removing watermarks, gridlines, and stamps.
Args:</p>
<blockquote>
<div><p>image (np.ndarray): Input image.
remove_watermark (bool): Flag to apply watermark removal.</p>
</div></blockquote>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>np.ndarray: Processed image.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.utils.enhance_image">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.utils.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">enhance_image</span></span></span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/utils.html#adaptive_threshold"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.utils.adaptive_threshold" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Enhance image by improving contrast and sharpness for OCR purposes.
Args:</p>
<blockquote>
<div><p>image (np.ndarray): Input image (BGR or grayscale).
        sharpen (bool): Whether to apply sharpening.
        contrast (bool): Whether to apply contrast enhancement using CLAHE.
        sharpening_method (str): Sharpening method ('unsharp_mask' or 'laplacian').
        amount (float): Sharpening strength (for unsharp_mask).
        kernel_size (int): Kernel size for blurring (for unsharp_mask).
        clip_limit (float): CLAHE clip limit.
        tile_grid_size (Union[tuple, list]): CLAHE tile grid size, can accept both tuple and list</p>
</div></blockquote>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>np.ndarray: Enhanced image.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.utils.denoise_advanced">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.utils.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">denoise_advanced</span></span></span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/utils.html#adaptive_threshold"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.utils.adaptive_threshold" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Apply denoising to an image using the specified method.
Args:</p>
<blockquote>
<div><p>image : np.ndarray
        Input image (grayscale or color).
    
    method : Literal["gaussian", "bilateral", "nl_means", "median"]
        Denoising method to apply.

    kernel_size : int, optional (default=5)
        Kernel size for Gaussian & Median filters. Must be an odd number.

    sigma_color : int, optional (default=75)
        Filter color variance for Bilateral filter.

    sigma_space : int, optional (default=75)
        Filter spatial variance for Bilateral filter.

    h : float, optional (default=10)
        Strength of Non-Local Means (NL-Means) denoising.

    template_window_size : int, optional (default=7)
        Template window size for NL-Means filter.

    search_window_size : int, optional (default=21)
        Search window size for NL-Means filter.</p>
</div></blockquote>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>np.ndarray: Denoised image.</p>
</dl>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Raises:</dt><dd><p>ValueError: If an invalid method or parameter is provided.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>


<dl class="py function">
<dt class="sig sig-object py" id="wissenai.preprocess.utils.threshold_advanced">
<span class="sig-prename descclassname"><span class="pre">wissenai.preprocess.utils.</span></span><span class="sig-name descname"><span class="pre">threshold_advanced</span></span></span><a class="reference internal" href="_modules/wissenai/preprocess/utils.html#adaptive_threshold"><span class="viewcode-link"><span class="pre">[source]</span></span></a><a class="headerlink" href="#wissenai.preprocess.utils.adaptive_threshold" title="Link to this definition"></a></dt>
<dd><p>Convert image to binary (black & white) using adaptive or Otsu's binarization.
Args:</p>
<blockquote>
<div><p>image (np.ndarray): Input image (BGR or grayscale).
        method (str): Binarization method - 'adaptive' or 'otsu'.
        block_size (int): Size of local neighborhood (odd integer) for adaptive method.
        C (int): Constant subtracted from the mean or weighted mean (adaptive only).</p>
</div></blockquote>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Returns:</dt><dd><p>np.ndarray: Binarized image (black & white).</p>
</dl>
<dl class="simple">
<dt>Raises:</dt><dd><p>ValueError: For invalid input or unsupported methods.</p>
</dd>
</dl>
</dd></dl>

